I asked you all for money to make lojban.org faster, and you
responded (more than I expected, thank you!), apparently on the
basis of me asserting that there was a problem.

I forgot something important, though, which was to ask *you* if you
think there's a problem.  I'm worried that I'm spending money to
solve a problem only I can see (because it's my professional field).

There are probably things I can do to make the server go faster, if
I worked hard at it, but let's say, for expediency's sake, that the
best I could do is to make it 25% faster than it is now.

Given that, what do you think?  Is lojban.org slow enough that I
should take people's money to make it better?

Thanks for your time.

-Robin

